H-OVERBLOCK, the PRICED version (Sharp's block search) — NOT SHIPPED: no win. Against main 56e9a80 (v6.15).
Instead of filtering block sets (spxoverblock.patch: Sharp -1.83, t -3.19), the search charges each
candidate set LA.obPrice life (env SPXLA_OBP) per hand card per determinization when a defence reaction
the seat can pay for alone covers what the set's armour leaves (non-lethal). Gate SPXOBPRICE; call key
laOverblock when the price flips the search's choice. Rule policy byte for byte (only laBlockSearch).
Own-seat A/B, Enigma's seat on Sharp vs the 14 others (rule policy), both seat orders, 28 games/seed,
12 seeds paired, wins of 28 (off 21.25):
  price 1: 21.25 -> 21.25 (+0.00, t 0.00)
  price 2: 21.25 -> 21.08 (-0.17, t -0.46)   per seed 22→22 20→20 22→20 22→23 22→21 21→21 23→21 20→19 24→25 18→17 20→21 21→23
  price 4: 21.25 -> 20.08 (-1.17, t -2.13)
Monotone: the more the waste is priced, the worse. The search's own block sets already beat both a ban
and a price — the "wasted" hand block is not waste on average (a guess: it keeps the reaction for a
later link or a bigger hit). 0 refusals / violations / stalls in every run. Ladder and phone bound not
run (not shipping). Apply: git apply experiments/spxobprice.patch
Suggest closing H-OVERBLOCK.

